# AI generation

- The platform should ask business questions and generate recommendations; users should not need to invent prompts.
- Use brand profile, audience, industry, goals, campaign, platform, and compliance context.
- Keep outputs editable and traceable.
- Do not claim content was published unless provider confirmation exists.
- Reserve credits before paid generation.
- Refund credits on definitive failure.
- Prevent duplicate charging through idempotency.
- Store provider job IDs and status transitions.
- Make asynchronous state visible: queued, generating, processing, completed, failed, cancelled.
- Prefer economical provider routing when quality is acceptable.
- Avoid hard-coding one provider where a provider-neutral adapter exists.
- Save completed media into the Media Library and working content into the Content Library when the established workflow requires it.
